   "unmapped": [
    "Learner picks one of M embedding models (K = M arms); the chosen model samples an item from a softmax over a low-rank (rank <= s) bilinear score; learner sees neither the model's distribution nor other models' recommendations",
    "Expected reward is (misspecified) bilinear in item and query, <Psi*, a q^T> + nu with |nu| <= epsilon",
    "Queries chosen by an adaptive adversary; regret fixes the realized queries",
    "Comparator is the log-quadratic softmax policy class pi(m|q) ∝ exp(q^T W_m q); linearized (Frank-Wolfe-gap) policy regret in parameter space"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "We frame the problem of routing queries to embedding models as a $T$-round adversarial contextual linear bandit with low-rank experts: In round $t$, the learner observes an adversarial query $q_t\\in \\mathbb{R}^{d_q}$ as \\emph{context} and faces an item set $\\mA\\subseteq \\mathbb R^{d_a}$ as \\emph{actions}. $M$ embedding models, as \\emph{experts}, each implicitly has a distribution over $\\mA$ via a latent embedding space of dimension $s\\ll \\min(d_q,d_a)$."
  },
